# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import lib/cadkernel/transform2.dl
import tests/cadkernel/cross2/input.dl

function emit transform2 curve {cad curve2:shape}:
    execute:
        emit measure2 scalar shape's kind
        if shape's kind = 0:
            emit measure2 point shape's line's start
            emit measure2 point shape's line's end
        if shape's kind = 1:
            emit measure2 point shape's circle's centre
            emit measure2 scalar shape's circle's radius
        if shape's kind = 2:
            emit measure2 point shape's arc's centre
            emit measure2 scalar shape's arc's radius
            emit measure2 scalar shape's arc's startAngle
            emit measure2 scalar shape's arc's endAngle
        if shape's kind = 3:
            emit measure2 point shape's ellipse's ellipse's centre
            emit measure2 scalar shape's ellipse's ellipse's majorRadius
            emit measure2 scalar shape's ellipse's ellipse's minorRadius
            emit measure2 point shape's ellipse's ellipse's majorAxis
            emit measure2 scalar shape's ellipse's startParameter
            emit measure2 scalar shape's ellipse's endParameter
        if shape's kind = 4:
            emit measure2 flag shape's polyline's closed
            emit measure2 scalar (the length of shape's polyline's vertices)
            loop index from 0 to the length of shape's polyline's vertices:
                set vertex to the item at index in shape's polyline's vertices
                emit measure2 point vertex's position
                emit measure2 scalar vertex's bulge
        if shape's kind = 5:
            emit measure2 scalar shape's nurbs's degree
            emit measure2 scalar (the length of shape's nurbs's controls)
            loop index from 0 to the length of shape's nurbs's controls:
                emit measure2 point (the item at index in shape's nurbs's controls)
            emit measure2 scalar (the length of shape's nurbs's knots)
            loop index from 0 to the length of shape's nurbs's knots:
                emit measure2 scalar (the item at index in shape's nurbs's knots)
            emit measure2 scalar (the length of shape's nurbs's weights)
            loop index from 0 to the length of shape's nurbs's weights:
                emit measure2 scalar (the item at index in shape's nurbs's weights)
        if shape's kind = 6:
            emit measure2 point shape's ray's origin
            emit measure2 point shape's ray's direction
        if shape's kind = 7:
            emit measure2 point shape's xline's base
            emit measure2 point shape's xline's direction

set mapping to a cad transform2 with axes (measure2 input point 1) and (measure2 input point 3) at (measure2 input point 5)
set shape to pair2 input curve at 7
set original to the cad clone of shape
emit measure2 scalar (the cad determinant of mapping)
emit measure2 flag (mapping preserves cad circles)
emit measure2 point (the cad image of (measure2 input point 10) under mapping)
emit measure2 point (the cad direction of (measure2 input point 10) under mapping)
set result to the cad transformed shape by mapping
emit measure2 flag result's valid
if result's valid:
    emit transform2 curve result's value
    set parameters to [-0.25,0.0,0.37,1.0,1.25]
    loop index from 0 to the length of parameters:
        set parameter to the item at index in parameters
        emit measure2 point (the cad point on result's value at parameter)
        emit measure2 point (the cad tangent of result's value at parameter)
emit measure2 flag (shape = original)
